 "notes": "Headline result: X-ray/gamma-ray exclusion on the ALP-electron coupling g_ae (light grey region of Fig. 2), derived by the authors from null results of NuSTAR M31, XMM-Newton blank-sky and INTEGRAL decaying-dark-matter line searches via the one-loop a->gamma gamma decay (Eqs. 2-4). Lagrangian Eq. (1) uses the canonical derivative coupling g_ae/(2 m_e) da ebar gamma^mu gamma5 e, so no conversion needed. Curve extracted from the vector PDF of Fig. 2 (combplDM.pdf in the e-print): lower boundary of the 30%-opacity grey polygon whose shape does NOT follow the tau=13.8 Gyr lifetime line (the other grey polygon follows g ~ m^-3.5 of Eq. 5 and is the dark-grey lifetime region). Axes calibrated from tick labels (x: 0.005-1 MeV log, y: 1e-21-1e-11 log); boundary path simplified with Douglas-Peucker (0.03 dex tolerance), preserving the narrow weak-limit notches near 5-12 keV visible in the figure. Curve spans the plotted range 4.96 keV to 0.98 MeV; paper quotes validity for m_a > 6 keV. Confidence level not stated in the paper; 95% assumed from the underlying telescope analyses. Limit assumes ALPs are all of the dark matter (galactic/M31 decay flux); no local-density rescaling applied.",
